Car Fuel Efficiency Predictor
========================================================
author: Dev Verma
date: October 27, 2026
autosize: true

A Shiny app that predicts a car's mileage and monthly fuel cost

The Problem
========================================================

- Buyers compare cars on price, but fuel cost adds up every month
- Mileage depends mainly on **weight**, **horsepower** and **transmission**
- People need a quick way to see how those specs change fuel efficiency and cost

**Our app:** move a few sliders, get predicted MPG, km/l and monthly fuel cost instantly.

The Model
========================================================

A linear regression on the built-in `mtcars` dataset:

```{r}
model <- lm(mpg ~ wt + hp + am, data = mtcars)
round(coef(model), 3)
round(summary(model)$r.squared, 3)
```

Each extra 1000 lbs of weight costs about 2.9 MPG, and the model explains about 84% of the variation in MPG.

Example Prediction
========================================================

A 3000 lb, 150 hp manual car:

```{r}
model <- lm(mpg ~ wt + hp + am, data = mtcars)
mpg <- predict(model, data.frame(wt = 3, hp = 150, am = 1))
kmpl <- mpg * 0.425144
c(MPG = round(mpg, 1), KmPerLitre = round(kmpl, 1),
  MonthlyCost = round(1000 / kmpl * 105))
```

The app does this calculation live as you move the sliders (1000 km/month at 105 per litre).

Try It
========================================================

- **App:** https://YOUR-USERNAME.shinyapps.io/MPGPredictor/
- **Code:** https://github.com/YOUR-USERNAME/MPGPredictor

Inputs: weight and horsepower sliders, transmission radio buttons, a fit-line checkbox, distance and fuel price.

Outputs: predicted MPG, km/l, monthly fuel cost, and a plot comparing your car with 32 others.

Full usage instructions are on the app's **Documentation** tab.
